# Spring Service Conventions — TokenRealty

Human doc: [docs/rules/spring-java-services.md](../../docs/rules/spring-java-services.md).  
Platform spec: [docs/PLATFORM-SPEC.md](../../docs/PLATFORM-SPEC.md).  
See also: [lombok.mdc](lombok.mdc), [java-dtos.mdc](java-dtos.mdc), [payment-ledger.mdc](payment-ledger.mdc), [investment-limits.mdc](investment-limits.mdc).

## Stack

- Java 21, Spring Boot 4, Maven
- PostgreSQL + JPA; Liquibase (forward-only when enabled)
- MapStruct + Lombok (entities/services/controllers — not rich domain models)
- Spring Security (JWT via shared `tokenrealty-security` library)
- Kafka + transactional outbox ([kafka-messaging.mdc](kafka-messaging.mdc))
- OpenAPI via springdoc

## Architecture — two layouts

### Layered (existing services)

Use for `token-realty-app`, `token-issuance-service`:

```text
com.tokenrealty.<service>/
├── controller/
├── service/
├── repository/
├── entity/
├── dto/
├── mapper/          (or inline mapping in service)
├── client/          (outbound RestClient to other services)
├── exception/
├── config/
└── kafka/           (event types, outbox, listeners)
```

Reference: Property Registry (`com.tokenrealty.registry`), Token Issuance (`com.tokenrealty.issuance`).

### Light hexagonal (new Tier 1+ services)

Use for `marketplace-service`, `auth-service`, `payment-service`, etc.:

```text
com.tokenrealty.<service>/
├── adapter/in/web/       REST controllers + request/response DTOs
├── adapter/in/kafka/     @KafkaListener (when consuming)
├── adapter/out/
│   ├── persistence/      JPA entities + repositories
│   ├── client/           RestClient implementations
│   └── kafka/            outbox publishers, relay
├── application/service/  use-case orchestration, @Transactional
├── application/port/out/ interfaces for DB, Kafka, external APIs (when extracting)
├── domain/               optional rich models (Payment, Marketplace)
├── dto/                  shared records (OK in layered style too)
├── exception/
├── config/
└── kafka/                OK at top level until full hexagonal split
```

**Marketplace reference:** `marketplace-service` — layered with `kafka/in/` (consumers), `kafka/outbox/` (publishers), `kafka/command/`; migrate to `adapter/*` incrementally.

Rules:

* Controllers: validate DTO → call service → map response. No repository, no business logic.
* Services: orchestrate use cases, own `@Transactional` boundaries.
* Do **not** hold DB transactions open during blockchain, IPFS, or HTTP calls to other services.
* External I/O (RestClient, Web3j, Hardhat subprocess) runs outside long `@Transactional` blocks when possible.
* Business rules live in services (layered) or domain (when extracted) — not in controllers or DTOs.

## Naming

* REST paths: plural nouns — `/v1/listings`, `/v1/orders`, `/v1/tokens`
* DTO records: `CreateListingRequest`, `ListingResponse`, grouped in `*Dtos.java` or per-feature records
* Services: `ListingService`, `OrderService`, `TokenIssuanceService`
* Clients: `PropertyRegistryClient`, `TokenIssuanceClient`
* Controllers: `ListingController`, `OrderController`
* IDs: `UUID` in API and JPA
* Money: `BigDecimal` with `precision = 19, scale = 2` on columns; use `RoundingMode.HALF_UP` for totals

## Package & port convention

| Service | Folder | Port | Context |
|---------|--------|------|---------|
| Property Registry | `token-realty-app/` | 8081 | `/api` |
| Token Issuance | `token-issuance-service/` | 8082 | `/api` |
| Auth | `auth-service/` | 8083 | `/api` |
| Marketplace | `marketplace-service/` | 8084 | `/api` |
| Payment | `payment-service/` | 8085 | `/api` |

Inter-service URLs in `application.yml`:

```yaml
services:
  auth:
    url: http://localhost:8083/api
  property-registry:
    url: http://localhost:8081/api
  token-issuance:
    url: http://localhost:8082/api
  marketplace:
    url: http://localhost:8084/api
  payment:
    url: http://localhost:8085/api
```

## Persistence

* JPA entities in `entity/` (layered) or `adapter/out/persistence/` (hexagonal).
* `@Version` on mutable aggregates — see `BaseEntity` in registry and marketplace.
* `@Enumerated(EnumType.STRING)` for new enum columns.
* Prefer LAZY associations; avoid EAGER unless justified.
* DB uniqueness via constraints + repository checks before insert.
* **Liquibase/Flyway forward-only** — never edit applied migrations; add a new changeset.
* Dev profile may use `hibernate.ddl-auto: update`; production uses Liquibase.

## Transaction boundaries

* `@Transactional(readOnly = true)` on service class; override with `@Transactional` on write methods.
* `@Transactional` on the **public** service method that commits the unit of work.
* Same-class internal calls do not pass through Spring proxy — fold logic into the public method.
* Outbox enqueue in the **same** transaction as the domain write ([kafka-messaging.mdc](kafka-messaging.mdc)).
* Never `KafkaTemplate.send` inside an uncommitted business transaction.

```java
// BAD — blockchain call inside TX
@Transactional
public OrderResponse placeOrder(PlaceOrderRequest req) {
    orderRepository.save(order);
    blockchain.transfer(...);  // slow; holds connection
    return response;
}

// GOOD — persist + outbox in TX; external calls after or in separate step
@Transactional
public OrderResponse placeOrder(PlaceOrderRequest req) {
    MarketOrder saved = orderRepository.save(order);
    eventPublisher.publishOrderMatched(saved, trade);
    return mapper.toOrderResponse(saved);
}
```

## Inter-service HTTP

* Outbound calls via dedicated `*Client` classes using `RestClient` ([rest-client-errors.mdc](rest-client-errors.mdc)).
* One `@Bean` RestClient per downstream base URL; inject with `@Qualifier`.
* Propagate `traceId` header when available.
* Service-to-service auth: Bearer JWT via `ServiceTokenProvider` + `tokenrealty-security` ([rest-client-errors.mdc](rest-client-errors.mdc)).
* Config: `services.<name>.url` — never hardcode URLs in services.

```java
// BAD — generic RestClient without qualifier
private final RestClient restClient;

// GOOD — marketplace-service
public TokenIssuanceClient(@Qualifier("tokenIssuanceRestClient") RestClient restClient)
```

## API

* OpenAPI 3 per service; Swagger UI at `/api/swagger-ui.html`
* Bean Validation (`@Valid`, `@NotNull`, `@NotBlank`) on request DTOs
* Errors: RFC 7807 `ProblemDetail` via `GlobalExceptionHandler`
* Standard codes/types:

```text
400  /errors/validation
401  unauthorized (Spring Security)
403  forbidden
404  /errors/not-found
409  /errors/conflict
422  /errors/business-rule
500  /errors/internal
```

* Typed exceptions: `ResourceNotFoundException`, `ConflictException`, `ValidationException`
* Use private `raiseException` helpers for repeated throws ([business-exception.mdc](business-exception.mdc))
* Financial/state-changing POST: `Idempotency-Key` header **required** on `POST /v1/payments` ([payment-ledger.mdc](payment-ledger.mdc))

## Paging

* All list endpoints support Spring `Pageable` ([pagination.mdc](pagination.mdc))
* Default size: 20 (`@PageableDefault(size = 20)`)
* Max size: 500 — clamp at controller if exposing raw `size` param
* Return `Page<ResponseDto>` directly

## Security

**Current:** JWT Bearer via shared `tokenrealty-security` library; login at Auth Service (:8083).

| Dev login | Role | Token |
|-----------|------|-------|
| admin@tokenrealty.com / admin123 | ADMIN | POST `/v1/auth/login` |
| investor@tokenrealty.com / investor123 | INVESTOR | same |
| token-issuance / issuance-secret | service ADMIN | POST `/v1/auth/service-token` |

Rules:

* Import `TokenRealtyJwtAutoConfiguration` in each service `SecurityConfig`; use `@Import` for `@WebMvcTest` slices.
* `@PreAuthorize` for fine-grained rules beyond HTTP method patterns.
* Inter-service RestClient: `ServiceTokenProvider` adds Bearer header when `tokenrealty.service-account.client-id` is set.
* Never log private keys, wallet seeds, or full KYC document content.

## Kafka & events

See [kafka-messaging.mdc](kafka-messaging.mdc) and [docs/EVENTS.md](../../docs/EVENTS.md).

* Topic pattern: `tokenrealty.{domain}.{aggregate}.{verb}.v1`
* Catalog in `*KafkaEventTypes`; sync with `application.yml`
* Outbox table per publishing service; relay when `tokenrealty.kafka.enabled=true`
* Consumers: idempotent on `eventId`; listener → one service call

## MapStruct & DTOs

* Java **records** for request/response DTOs, commands, events
* MapStruct in `mapper/` package, or manual mapper `@Component` (marketplace uses manual)
* Do not expose JPA entities from controllers
* Records for DTOs; Lombok `@Builder` on entities

## Testing

| Layer | Approach |
|-------|----------|
| Service unit | JUnit 5 + Mockito; no Spring context |
| Controller slice | `@WebMvcTest` + `@Import(SecurityConfig)` |
| Integration | `@SpringBootTest` + `@ActiveProfiles("test")` + H2 |
| Full stack | Testcontainers PostgreSQL (+ Kafka when wired) |

Run: `./mvnw test` per service module.

## Observability

* Spring Actuator: `/actuator/health`, `/actuator/info`, `/actuator/metrics`
* Structured logs; include `traceId` when propagating
* Target: Prometheus + OpenTelemetry (Phase 5)

## Documentation per service

Each service module requires:

* `README.md` — quick start, port, API table, test users
* Swagger/OpenAPI (springdoc)
* Link to [docs/PLATFORM-SPEC.md](../../docs/PLATFORM-SPEC.md) for platform context

## Controller rules

```java
// BAD — business logic in controller
@PostMapping
public OrderResponse place(@RequestBody PlaceOrderRequest req) {
    if (req.tokenAmount() < 10) throw ...
    listing.setTokensAvailable(...);
}

// GOOD
@PostMapping
public OrderResponse place(@Valid @RequestBody PlaceOrderRequest req) {
    return orderService.placeBuyOrder(req);
}
```

## Configuration

* `@ConfigurationProperties` for typed service config (prefer over scattered `@Value`)
* Secrets from environment — `OPERATOR_PRIVATE_KEY`, `DB_PASSWORD`, never committed
* Profiles: `local`, `test`, `staging`, `prod`

## Sensitive domain rules (real estate / crypto)

* KYC gate before token purchase — call Token Issuance `/v1/compliance/check/{wallet}`
* Token transfer and payment must be reconcilable (order ↔ trade ↔ payment ↔ txHash)
* Dividends: pro-rata by ownership %; immutable payout records once SETTLED
* Property status sync: `TransferCompleted` → registry flat status (`FULLY_SOLD` when applicable)

## When adding a new microservice

1. Copy structure from `marketplace-service/` or `payment-service/` (pom, JWT security, exception handler, outbox)
2. Assign port from [PLATFORM-SPEC.md](../../docs/PLATFORM-SPEC.md) §7
3. Create PostgreSQL database `{service_name}` with underscores
4. Add README + link in [docs/README.md](../../docs/README.md)
5. Add Kafka event types to [docs/EVENTS.md](../../docs/EVENTS.md) if publishing/consuming
6. Follow [kafka-messaging.mdc](kafka-messaging.mdc) for events
